# Section images: real photography only

Hard rule for diana’s dashboard (`/Users/diana/my-dashboard`) **section / zone / vision-tile** images — whenever assigning, generating, finding, or swapping a section photo.

Broader than `no-other-faces-or-names` (faces + third-party names). This rule also bans AI-look photorealism, cinematic/fantasy lighting, and non-photo media. Do **not** weaken the faces/names rule; both apply. Rejected photos never return — see `rejected-section-photos-banned`.

## Criteria checklist (all must pass)

When assigning an image to a **section**:

1. **Actual-looking photography only** — real camera stills (environments, objects, documents, places) — except where an exception below explicitly allows conceptual / luminous imagery
2. **No AI-style photorealism** — plastic skin, over-smooth texture, fake “perfect” stills that read as generated
3. **No cinematic or fantasy lighting** — god-rays, stage fog, neon glow drama, movie-grade color grade (except conceptual exceptions below)
4. **No surreal / impossible scenes** — floating objects, dream logic, compositing that could not be a real photo (except conceptual exceptions below)
5. **No illustrations or digital art** — drawings, 3D renders, paintings, vector art, concept art (except conceptual exceptions below)
6. **No faces / identifiable humans** — no faces, no photoreal people, no skin detail that reads as a real person. **Silhouettes are OK** (shadow-figures, pure black outline forms). When a silhouette is used, it must be a **woman’s** silhouette — see `woman-silhouettes-only`

## Always

1. Prefer plain documentary light over dramatic grade
2. Conceptual sections (soul, sorrow, darkness, abundance, attention, etc.) stay object/environment still-lifes **or** woman silhouettes when that reads clearer. **soul ≠ sorrow** — never treat them as aliases or share one photo under both names (see `rejected-section-photos-banned`). **Abundance wheat/plenty2 is rejected** — leave nophoto rather than restoring wheat or assigning AI cinematic surplus (see `rejected-section-photos-banned`)
3. Keep `everything.html` + `prototype.html` + `serve.py` in sync when shipping a section photo
4. Bump `?v=` + migration `MKEY` when forcing a scrub so stale assets cannot win

## Exceptions (only these)

- **User-provided screenshots** — use **as-is**, unaltered. Do not regenerate, restyle, or “fix” toward this rule
- **Audacity finger silhouette** — Diana-supplied; do **not** ban or replace it in a cleanup migration. Do **not** treat other silhouettes as “like audacity”
- **to channel** — quantum / biofield / shared luminous field imagery is allowed (abstract luminous field OK). Prefer imagery that reads as **shared energy / biofield / souls in the same field** — woman silhouettes in one field are OK and preferred when abstract alone does not read. Do **not** “fix” it back to literal real photography (irrigation canal, etc.). Still: no faces, no other people’s names
- **Woman silhouettes** — allowed on sections when they help the concept land; must follow `woman-silhouettes-only` (never masculine / gender-ambiguous)

## If a new section photo violates this

Replace it immediately with imagery that meets the criteria. Do not ask permission. Do not leave faces or masculine silhouettes live.
